.TH "OPEN-IN-FIREFOX" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
open\-in\-firefox \- launch Firefox installed as a Flatpak
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBopen\-in\-firefox [FIREFOX\-ARG...]\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Forward all arguments to flatpak run org.mozilla.firefox. The chezmoi template creates this executable only when Linux, flatpak and the Firefox Flatpak are detected during template rendering.
.SH NOTES
This wrapper is conditional and might not exist on hosts without the Firefox Flatpak.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires Linux with flatpak installed and the
org.mozilla.firefox Flatpak present at chezmoi template-rendering
time. The wrapper is conditional and might not be generated
on a host that lacks either prerequisite.
.SH OPERATION
The wrapper simply runs flatpak run org.mozilla.firefox, forwarding
every argument verbatim. It does not select native Firefox,
install the Flatpak, or handle an absent runtime dynamically.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
flatpak info org.mozilla.firefox
open-in-firefox https://example.org
open-in-firefox --private-window https://example.org
.fi
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
If this command is missing after installing Firefox Flatpak,
regenerate or reapply the chezmoi configuration so the template
can detect the newly available application.
